OL,3,ASchools not ready for AI and 'crying
OL,4,Aout' for government guidance, report
OL,5,Awarns
OL,6,
OL,7,FSchools are "crying out" for guidance
OL,8,Ffrom government on how pupils and
OL,9,Fteachers can use AI safely and
OL,10,Feffectively, a new report has warned.
OL,12,FSir Anthony Seldon, former head teacher
OL,13,Fand author on AI in education, says the
OL,14,Ftechnology is being used more and more
OL,15,Ffrequently, but that its introduction
OL,16,Fhas been "chaotic and anarchic".
